    "summary": "Belum (image of a tew, i.e., malevolent spirit) (with separate arms and spear); carved of sago palm pith; a) body: male human figure, seated with knees drawn up to body, crown on head, cross-hatching on face, triangles and semicircles carved on chest, chevrons on legs; b) right arm with hand curled to hold end of spear; c) left arm with hand curled to hold tip of spear; d) model spear: rounded handle with flat blade of spear carved to point; to be held with point downward in left hand, handle in right hand; represents the water spirit Dalong Bau Batang.",
